meta {
  name: 16-Accept the assignment (BLOCKED — needs an invite from Biodun)
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/api/agent-listings/{{emeka_pending_assignment_id}}/accept
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{emeka_jwt}}
}

assert {
  res.status: in [200, 400, 404, 403, 401]
}

docs {
  If Biodun has invited me, this transitions REQUESTED → ACCEPTED
  and the owner gets notified.

  Solo run: emeka_pending_assignment_id is unset, so the request
  hits an invalid path. The 404/403 is expected — keeping this in
  the collection so when the orchestrator wires Biodun in, the call
  works end-to-end.

  GAP I'd flag even on success: there's no way for me to send the
  owner a short note like "got it, I'm on this" alongside accept.
  Owner just gets a system notification. For trust-building, that's
  cold.
}
